### **20.6.5 Combining bullet chart and sparklines**

Similarly, we can combining the bullet chart and sparklines using the steps below.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
bullet <- coffeechain %>%
  filter(Date >= "2013-01-01") %>%
  group_by(`Product`) %>%
  summarise(`Target` = sum(`Budget Sales`),
            `Actual` = sum(`Sales`)) %>%
  ungroup()  
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sales_data = sales_data %>%
  left_join(bullet)
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sales_data %>%
  gt() %>%
  gt_plt_sparkline(
    column = "Monthly Sales",
    type = "points",
    same_limit = FALSE,
    palette = c("white", "white", "purple", "green", "white")
  ) %>%
  gt_plt_bullet(
    column = Actual,
    target = Target,
    width = 28,
    palette = c("lightblue", "black")
  ) %>%
  gt_theme_538()
```

