## **Exploration**

**1) Target Achievement Analysis using Bullet Charts**

Identify products that exceeded expectations and those that underperformed relative to their sales targets.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
target_perf <- coffeechain %>%
  filter(Date >= "2013-01-01") %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarise(
    Target = sum(`Budget Sales`, na.rm = TRUE),
    Actual = sum(Sales, na.rm = TRUE),
    Achievement = Actual / Target,
    .groups = "drop"
  ) %>%
  arrange(desc(Achievement))

target_perf %>%
  gt() %>%
  fmt_percent(
    columns = Achievement,
    decimals = 1
  ) %>%
  gt_plt_bullet(
    column = Actual,
    target = Target,
    width = 35,
    palette = c("lightblue", "black")
  ) %>%
  gt_theme_538()
```

